instructions:
For layout, use the Row and Column components to organize other components.

## Catalog Guidelines

1. String Concatenation & Formatting: A2UI does not support binary operators like '+' or formatting symbols. To concatenate strings or dynamically inject data bindings into text, you must use the catalog function `formatString(value)` where the value string contains placeholders formatted as `${expression}`:
   formatString("Hello ${/user/name}")

2. Strict Hierarchy: You must strictly adhere to the requested component nesting and hierarchy. If the prompt specifies that a component is 'inside' or 'contained in' another component, you MUST place it as a child of that specific component, not as a sibling or in a different container.

3. Validation Checks: When components support validation checks, specify any custom error messages directly as the 'message' inside the check. Do NOT create separate text-display components to display validation errors.

## Examples

Example 1: Dynamic text form
```json
[
  {
    "version": "1.0",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "main",
      "catalogId": "https://a2ui.org/specification/v1_0/catalogs/basic/catalog.json",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "Column",
          "children": ["repField", "valueField"]
        },
        {
          "id": "repField",
          "component": "TextField",
          "label": "Representative",
          "value": {"@path": "/form/rep"},
          "placeholder": "Enter name"
        },
        {
          "id": "valueField",
          "component": "TextField",
          "label": "Deal Value",
          "value": {"@path": "/form/value"},
          "placeholder": "0.00",
          "variant": "number",
          "checks": [
            {
              "condition": {
                "@call": "required",
                "args": {"value": {"@path": "/form/value"}}
              },
              "message": "Deal value is required."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "dataModel": {
        "form": {
          "rep": "John Doe",
          "value": 1500.00
        }
      }
    }
  }
]
```

Example 2: Dynamic list with templates
```json
[
  {
    "version": "1.0",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "main",
      "catalogId": "https://a2ui.org/specification/v1_0/catalogs/basic/catalog.json",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "Card",
          "child": "breedList"
        },
        {
          "id": "breedList",
          "component": "List",
          "children": {
            "path": "/breeds",
            "componentId": "breedTemplate"
          },
          "direction": "horizontal"
        },
        {
          "id": "breedTemplate",
          "component": "Image",
          "url": {"@path": "url"}
        }
      ],
      "dataModel": {
        "breeds": [
          {
            "url": "https://example.com/poodle.jpg"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://example.com/lab.jpg"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
]
```

## Charts and data

Draw numbers as charts, not prose: PieChart for shares, LineChart for a trend over time, BarChart to compare categories, Metric for one key figure, DataTable for rows. Put the rows in the data model and bind them, so a later update can change the data alone. Group charts in Cards inside a Row or Column for a dashboard. Leave colors out to use the theme palette. For a list of like cards (one per alert, product or account), use a Grid with a template child: Grid(_template($/alerts, alertCard)); the cards wrap into equal columns instead of stretching across the pane. To offer per-card actions without crowding the card, put one HoverBar of borderless Buttons anywhere in it: it shows in the cell's top-right corner while the pointer is over the card (every HoverBar in a cell takes that corner, so give each card one). To let the user add to the list, end the Grid with an AddCard rather than a separate button: Grid(_template($/alerts, alertCard), after=addAlert), addAlert = AddCard("Add alert", Event("add_alert")).

Title a dashboard with Heading (level 1 for the page, 3 for a card); its subtitle is the small line under it. Show a status with Badge, or give a DataTable column a badge map so each cell is one. Put a chart's unit (its value axis, a pie's legend, the tooltip) in valuePrefix / valueSuffix rather than in the numbers.

Give a Metric better: "down" when a rise is bad (refund rate, churn, latency), so its delta is coloured by meaning. To let the user ask about a change where it is shown, give the Metric an action and an actionLabel, e.g. action=Event("explain_metric", {metric: "Refund rate"}), actionLabel="Ask why"; the action comes back to you like a Button press. A Metric's action is optional: leave both out on a plain figure, and never give it a placeholder Event("click").

Example 3: Sales dashboard
```json
[
  {
    "version": "1.0",
    "createSurface": {
      "surfaceId": "sales",
      "catalogId": "https://velloc.app/a2ui/catalog/v1",
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "component": "Column",
          "children": [
            "total",
            "charts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "total",
          "component": "Metric",
          "label": "Revenue",
          "value": {
            "@path": "/total"
          },
          "delta": "+12%",
          "trend": "up"
        },
        {
          "id": "charts",
          "component": "Row",
          "children": [
            "shareCard",
            "trendCard"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "shareCard",
          "component": "Card",
          "child": "share",
          "weight": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "share",
          "component": "PieChart",
          "title": "By region",
          "data": {
            "@path": "/regions"
          },
          "donut": true
        },
        {
          "id": "trendCard",
          "component": "Card",
          "child": "trend",
          "weight": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "trend",
          "component": "LineChart",
          "title": "Monthly",
          "data": {
            "@path": "/months"
          },
          "xKey": "month",
          "series": [
            {
              "key": "sales",
              "label": "Sales"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "dataModel": {
        "total": "$980K",
        "regions": [
          {
            "label": "North",
            "value": 45
          },
          {
            "label": "South",
            "value": 30
          }
        ],
        "months": [
          {
            "month": "Jan",
            "sales": 120
          },
          {
            "month": "Feb",
            "sales": 150
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
]
```

Give a tab a badge for a count that needs attention, e.g. {title: "Inbox", child: inbox, badge: $/inbox/count}; a badge of 0 or no value is hidden, so bind it rather than leaving it out. Use open=1 (zero-based) to show a tab other than the first when the surface is drawn.
